 with vigilance.', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Intrusive Packbeast enters the battlefield, tap up to two target creatures your opponents control.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Swathcutter Giant attacks, it deals 1 damage to each creature defending player controls.', "Vigilance\\n{T}, Sacrifice Bounty Agent: Destroy target legendary permanent that's an artifact, creature, or enchantment.", "When Affectionate Indrik enters the battlefield, you may have it fight target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "When Attendant of Vraska dies, if you control a Vraska planeswalker, you gain life equal to Attendant of Vraska's power.", 'When Burglar Rat enters the battlefield, each opponent discards a card.', 'When Centaur Peacemaker enters the battlefield, each player gains 4 life.', 'When Dimir Informant enters the battlefield, surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', "When Disinformation Campaign enters the battlefield, you draw a card and each opponent discards a card.\\nWhenever you surveil, return Disinformation Campaign to its owner's hand.", 'When District Guide enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card or Gate card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Generous Stray enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Glowspore Shaman enters the battlefield, mill three cards. You may put a land card from your graveyard on top of your library. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', 'When Golgari Findbroker enters the battlefield, return target permanent card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Guild Summit enters the battlefield, you may tap any number of untapped Gates you control. Draw a card for each Gate tapped this way.\\nWhenever a Gate enters the battlefield under your control, draw a card.', 'When Hunted Witness dies, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', 'When Ironshell Beetle enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'When Knight of Autumn enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Put two +1/+1 counters on Knight of Autumn.\\n• Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n• You gain 4 life.', "When Lazav, the Multifarious enters the battlefield, surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)\\n{X}: Lazav, the Multifarious becomes a copy of target creature card in your graveyard with mana value X, except its name is Lazav, the Multifarious, it's legendary in addition to its other types, and it has this ability.", "When Plaguecrafter enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature or planeswalker. Each player who can't discards a card.", 'When Rubblebelt Boar enters the battlefield, target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'When Spinal Centipede dies, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.', 'When Sumala Woodshaper enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature or enchantment card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'When Tenth District Guard enters the battlefield, target creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Emmara, Soul of the Accord becomes tapped, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', "Whenever Goblin Locksmith attacks, creatures with defender can't block this turn.", 'Whenever Haazda Marshal and at least two other creatures attack, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', 'Whenever Inspiring Unicorn attacks, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Ledev Champion attacks, you may tap any number of untapped creatures you control. Ledev Champion gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature tapped this way.\\n{3}{G}{W}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', 'Whenever Ornery Goblin blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Ornery Goblin deals 1 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever Skyline Scout attacks, you may pay {1}{W}. If you do, it gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever Vedalken Mesmerist attacks, target creature an opponent controls gets -2/-0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, Midnight Reaper deals 1 damage to you and you draw a card.', "Whenever another creature you control enters the battlefield or dies, if that creature's power is greater than Pelt Collector's, put a +1/+1 counter on Pelt Collector.\\nAs long as Pelt Collector has three or more +1/+1 counters on it, it has trample.", 'Whenever you cast a blue spell, target player mills two cards.', 'Whenever you cast a creature spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast a red spell, if Runaway Steam-Kin has fewer than three +1/+1 counters on it, put a +1/+1 counter on Runaway Steam-Kin.\\nRemove three +1/+1 counters from Runaway Steam-Kin: Add {R}{R}{R}.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell that targets only Beamsplitter Mage, if you control one or more other creatures that spell could target, choose one of those creatures. Copy that spell. The copy targets the chosen creature.', "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, copy it for each other instant and sorcery spell you've cast before it this turn. You may choose new targets for the copies.", 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 blue Bird Illusion creature token with flying.', "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, put a charge counter on Firemind's Research.\\n{1}{U}, Remove two charge counters from Firemind's Research: Draw a card.\\n{1}{R}, Remove five charge counters from Firemind's Research: It deals 5 damage to any target.", "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, target creature an opponent controls can't block this turn.", 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.\\n{3}{W}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', 'Whenever you surveil for the first time each turn, Whispering Snitch deals 1 damage to each opponent and you gain 1 life.', 'You gain X life and draw X cards, where X is the number of creatures you control. Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'You may look at an additional two cards each time you surveil.\\nExile Enhanced Surveillance: Shuffle your graveyard into your library.', "You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may play lands and cast spells from the top of your library.\\nYou can't play lands or cast spells from your hand.\\n{3}{R}: Destroy Experimental Frenzy.", '[+1]: Draw a card.\\n[−2]: Ral, Caller of Storms deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.\\n[−7]: Draw seven cards. Ral, Caller of Storms deals 7 damage to each creature your opponents control.', '[+1]: Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other into your graveyard.\\n[−3]: Ral, Izzet Viceroy deals damage to target creature equal to the total number of instant and sorcery cards you own in exile and in your graveyard.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this emblem deals 4 damage to any target and you draw two cards."', '[+2]: Put a +1/+1 counter on up to one target creature. That creature gains menace until end of turn.\\n[−3]: Destroy target creature.\\n[−10]: For each creature card in your graveyard, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', '[+2]: You may sacrifice another permanent. If you do, you gain 1 life and draw a card.\\n[−3]: Destroy target nonland permanent with mana value 3 or less.\\n[−9]: You get an emblem with "Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, that player loses the game."', '{1}, Sacrifice Goblin Cratermaker: Choose one —\\n• Goblin Cratermaker deals 2 damage to target creature.\\n• Destroy target colorless nonland permanent.', "{1}, Sacrifice another creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Undercity Necrolisk. It gains menace until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", '{1}{B}: Veiled Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{1}{U}, {T}: Target creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\\n{2}{B}, {T}: Surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)", '{2}{U}, {T}: You may cast an instant or sorcery spell from your hand without paying its mana cost.', "{2}{U}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{3}{U}, {T}: Draw a card.\\n{X}{R}, {T}: Copy target instant or sorcery spell you control with mana value X. You may choose new targets for the copy.', '{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Silent Dart: It deals 3 damage to target creature.', "{4}{B}, {T}: Creatures you control get +1/+0 and gain menace until end of turn. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\n{1}{G}, {T}: You gain 2 life.", '{4}{G}: Devkarin Dissident gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{5}{R}, {T}: Legion Guildmage deals 3 damage to each opponent.\\n{2}{W}, {T}: Tap another target creature.', '{G}, {T}: Creatures you control gain trample until end of turn.\\n{5}{W}, {T}: Create a 2/2 green and white Elf Knight creature token with vigilance.', '{T}: Add {B} or {G}.\\n{B/G}{B/G}{B/G}{B/G}, {T}, Sacrifice Golgari Locket: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color. If that mana is spent on a multicolored creature spell, that creature enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', '{T}: Add {G} or {W}.\\n{G/W}{G/W}{G/W}{G/W}, {T}, Sacrifice Selesnya Locket: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {R} or {W}.\\n{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}, {T}, Sacrifice Boros Locket: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {U} or {B}.\\n{U/B}{U/B}{U/B}{U/B}, {T}, Sacrifice Dimir Locket: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {U} or {R}.\\n{U/R}{U/R}{U/R}{U/R}, {T}, Sacrifice Izzet Locket: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Mill a card.\\n{2}, {T}, Exile Wand of Vertebrae: Shuffle up to five target cards from your graveyard into your library.']
flavor: ['"A massive new Izzet building project with an unstated purpose? Probably fine."\\n—Zija, Simic mutationist', '"Article 5.8.2. Ensure proper restraint of any and all arms, legs, claws, jaws, tails, tentacles, and tendrils as appropriate."\\n—*Azorius Arrester Procedure*, Appendix B', '"Bats are welcome to eat thousands of my pets. I have multitudes more that will ultimately eat the bats."\\n—Izoni', '"Be advised: suspect is nine stories tall, marble hair, answers to Saint Gusztav."', '"Be like the grazers of the Saruli. Keep your herd close, and stay alert for encroaching danger."\\n—Lalia, Selesnya dryad', '"Before I let you wield one of these, let\'s see you dodge one!"', '"By all means, take another step toward the captain."', '"Commander, we caught the Dimir spy and took her ashes into custody."\\n—Kramm, Wojek security officer', '"Commander, what\'s the signal to attack?"\\n"You\'ll know."', '"Countermagic is a simple process of breaking matter into its elementary particles."', '"Don\'t arrest him—enlist him!"\\n—Commander Yaszen', '"Don\'t stop till your horns come out their back."', '"Even rats hoard their treasures. Are your precious things so different?"\\n—Izoni', '"Every guild dreads infiltration. I should know—I\'ve been a member of all of them."\\n—Lazav', '"Everyone who crosses that threshold is our most cherished friend. Everyone who crosses it again is our bitterest enemy."\\n—Trostani', '"He\'s got more finesse than most goblins. He smashes windows with his fist rather than his forehead."\\n—Arrester Polgar', '"Hold on to your ideals. They\'ll be tested more than your armor or the edge of your blade."\\n—Tajic', '"How thoughtful of the Legion to train its soldiers to fit our spell\'s specifications."\\n—Nefara, Dimir agent', '"I am the very soul of battle, but even I would never advise open war with the Conclave."\\n—Aurelia', '"I long for peaceful times, when I may tend to my garden instead of our borders."', '"I packed three more electroconduits into each test wand. You\'ll experience a brief tingling sensation."', '"I prefer the big and looming to the small and skittering."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"I sang songs of sorrow for my lost love. Imagine my horror when, one night, they were answered."\\n—Milana, Orzhov prelate', '"I spent some time in the Legion, but I\'m done taking orders all day."', '"I\'ve raised her since she was a pup, and she\'s raised me since I was a recruit."', '"I\'ve seen Ravnica\'s fate. Believe me, I\'m doing you a favor."', '"I\'ve seen your house, and you\'ve been a lovely, if unwitting, host. But at last it\'s time for farewells."', '"It is not your time. The Legion still needs your blade."', '"It is our duty to protect all those in need. But the other guilds have never shown themselves worthy of that protection."\\n—Tajic', '"It\'s both an ingress-denial mechanism and an attractive hallway light!"\\n—Daxiver, Izzet electromancer', '"It\'s like blowing up an arcane library in a thermobaric explosion. But in a good way."\\n—Bori Andon, Izzet blastseeker', '"It\'s truly the highest honor, isn\'t it? To be remembered? Pity for you."', '"Jarad was a friend to the Devkarin. Now we slink through neglected tunnels, befriending those who crawl them."\\n—Izoni', '"Just as leaves fall and the tree blooms again, one day I will fall and the Conclave will endure."', '"Lately I\'ve seen the biggest bounties of my career—and for the biggest names."', '"Laws apply only to those who lack the vision to see past them."', '"Light a torch and deliver this letter" were his instructions, which he unfortunately reversed.', '"Light up the dark to find your way, and the dark may seek you out."\\n—Zalin the Gutter Bard', '"Most compete for insects at street level. Some dwell near Izzet laboratories and ride the thermal updrafts."\\n—Yolov, Simic bioengineer', '"My doors are called trespassing, my signatures, forgeries. They don\'t respect my talents, and I don\'t respect their labels."', '"My greatest creation—me!"', '"My power is generosity, in a way. I give my survivors an appreciation for their lives."', '"My specialty is theoretical universal limits and ways to circumvent them."', '"Nobody ever listens to my complaints! Not even when I use the listening stick."', '"Not my first edition of *The Advokist and the Urchin*!"', '"Now do you understand what we meant when we said *disperse*?"\\n—Eksari, Boros patrol leader', '"Now it\'s your turn to hide."\\n—Vraska', '"Oh, you fellas are going to love the lockup. Excellent gruel. Very low ceilings."\\n—Libuse, Boros sergeant', '"Our forces number more than the leaves of Vitu-Ghazi. Do not provoke us."', '"People would sooner savor sweet lies than chew plain truths."\\n—Lazav', '"Please accept this offering. I sincerely hope to leave my mace at my side."', '"Please don\'t feed the beetles."\\n—Promenade warning sign', '"Remember to discharge your locket every seven hours. Unless you prefer the spontaneous aether overload, of course."\\n—Daxiver, Izzet electromancer', '"Reports of Gruul rioters in four districts. Start with the big ones and work your way up."\\n—Libuse, Boros sergeant', '"Result 752: Rapid mass redistribution.\\n"Result 753: Calamitous reverse synthesis.\\n"Result 754: Acute disarrayment."\\n—Izzet research notes', '"Selesnya\'s soil is sacred, and you\'re about to meet it with your face."', '"Send your champion. I could use a light workout."', '"Shut the gates. In the Underrealm we will outlast the coming doom."\\n—Vraska', '"Something\'s causing electrospheric disruption in the blazekite\'s spire-vanes. Find the cause, and tell them to keep it up!"\\n—Juzba, Izzet tinker', '"Sometimes an angel passes by and gives me a little nod, like, \'You\'re a daring one!\' That always makes my day."', '"Sure, I hear things. I hear plenty. But how am I to talk with this parched throat?"', '"The Dimir may look all they want. We never grow tired of swatting their bugs."\\n—Heruj, Selesnya hierophant', '"The Erstwhile—rotten of body and outmoded in dress, but unfailing in loyalty."\\n—Vraska', '"The Golgari believe they should be given what they deserve. On this we agree."\\n—Tajic', '"The Izzet are blamed for every little disaster, which is unfair because we only cause most of them."\\n—Mizzix of the Izmagnus', '"The League accepts no responsibility for former members and the damage they may cause."\\n—Maree, Izzet chamberlain', '"The Tenth has always been my home. This city is constantly embroiled in one crisis or another, but I\'m determined to protect my piece."', '"The alliances were already frayed. All we do is find the loose threads and pluck."\\n—Lazav', '"The dagger is just the distraction. I carry the real killer in a vial at my side."', '"The dead gain new purpose here. What is strange in the eyes of other guilds is harmonious in ours."\\n—Devesh, Golgari shaman', '"The more trust breaks down, the more we must throw open the front gates."\\n—Aurelia', '"The reign of the Swarm begins. Let us rise now and dress ourselves in vengeance."', '"The route is direct but challenging. Incidentally, how are you with heights?"', '"The shortest path between two points is not always the safest."\\n—Tamina, district guide', '"The tiniest mouse speaks louder to me than all the festival crowds on Tin Street."', '"The trouble with youths these days is that, in outright defiance of their elders, they refuse to be bought."\\n—Karlov of the Ghost Council', '"There is nothing stronger than many hearts united for a single cause."\\n—Emmara', '"There\'s no need to sound the alarm. You are minding your post admirably. I am authorized. All is well."', '"These terms are acceptable to House Dimir. Shall we shake on it?"', '"They don\'t even feel the cut. I\'m ordering a drink in a nearby tavern before anyone notices something\'s wrong."', '"They play by spitting fire at each other. Don\'t be offended if one gives you a love-scorch."\\n—Esfir, Rakdos dragon wrangler', '"They said obey and you\'ll be happy. They said you\'ll be safe. But we\'re not safe. We\'re not happy. And we will not obey."\\n—Domri Rade', '"They tell us the wilds are ours, then they brick them over. They can lie to our faces but not to our fists."\\n—Ghut Rak, Gruul guildmage', '"Think of the locket as a seed you bear, spreading life from Vitu-Ghazi across all of Ravnica."\\n—Heruj, Selesnya hierophant', '"This is Mileva, in the Tenth. We\'ve got an elf in the plaza with a chip on her shoulder. Actually, it\'s more of a morningstar."', '"This sort of innovation occurs when you set out to improve an electric tea kettle and misplace a decimal."', '"Those who show no mercy to the weak deserve no mercy from the strong."\\n—Firemane Kavrova', '"Three daggers left in an angel\'s back, three enforcers with memory loss, three keys stolen from my own belt—and you talk of peace?"\\n—Tajic, to Aurelia', '"To wage war, secure peace within yourself."\\n—Emmara', '"Too many have disappeared in these dark days. I am the light that will lead them home."', '"Variety is also the spice of death."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"Watch carefully. The gap between death and victory is thinner than your blade."', '"We are the shield that never breaks, the bough that never burns, the song that can never be silenced."', '"We gather the past from surface dwellers and sell it right back to them."', '"We have intel that some guilds have fallen under an invader\'s influence. Until we\'re sure, no venture succeeds."\\n—Lazav', '"We leave our gardens open, so all may know wonder, but guarded, so all may know peace."\\n—Emmara', '"We pass these along to our fellow soldiers to recognize deeds of valor. It won\'t stay with you for long."\\n—Alovnek, Boros guildmage', '"We\'re on the fortieth floor, with one window, no balcony. No one could possibly get in."\\n—Minosz, Orzhov chief of security', '"Wear it at all times. It will guide our reanimators to your corpse."\\n—Mazirek, kraul death priest', '"Wear this, and take your place among the shadows—wise, lethal, and unseen."\\n—Ivrelya, Dimir spymaster', '"What bait do you cast to catch a dream?"\\n—Ravnican riddle', '"What wishes do they grant? Mostly pinching-related ones."\\n—Omik, superintendent of waterworks', '"Whatever hatred destroys, a single act of trust can revive."', '"Where the roots reach, there the temple rises."\\n—Niszka, Selesnya evangel', '"Who are the agents of the Dimir? No one and everyone."\\n—Lazav', '"Within the song of Mat\'Selesnya, one becomes all."\\n—Heruj, Selesnya hierophant', '"Yes, there\'s competition between our equenauts and the Boros skyjeks. At least they think it\'s a competition."', '"Yesterday I didn\'t recognize my own guild. Today I see why. And for tomorrow I must be prepared."\\n—Niv-Mizzet', '"You will not be trained here. You will be forged."\\n—Commander Yaszen', '"You won\'t need the sword drills, your shields, or my blessing. You\'ll fight for Sunhome with the truth in your heart."\\n—Aurelia', '"You\'ve found this place only because you were summoned. Pray you\'re worthy of the invitation."\\n—Etrata', '"You\'ve strayed, overworlder."', 'A composer wrote a symphony based on the drakes screeching outside her window. Reviews were mixed—except among the drakes.', 'A power vacuum for the Azorius. A keepsake for Vraska.', 'A swiftblade is an artist, each fiery trail of their blades a fleeting masterpiece traced on the air.', 'A well-chosen word can restore a mind or snap its tethers.', 'All things considered, his first day on patrol could have gone better.', 'All those who trade in questions must answer to the Dimir.', "Beneath Ravnica's streets runs a layer of tunnels, then caverns and waterways, then terrors and nightmares.", 'By guild tradition, any puddle of multicolored light on the cobblestones can serve as neutral ground.', 'Cats place their gifts with care, so that a bare foot will step on them in the middle of the night.', 'City air is a constant drizzle of private thoughts.', "Cradle of the Golgari's new kingdom. Grave of those who wronged its queen.", 'Dimir assassinations are choreographed like dance routines. Each challenge is anticipated and countered with graceful ease.', 'Dimir assassins have the precision to slay a single memory.', 'Each night it visits a different guildgate around the city, digging its talons into fresh stone.', "Every laboratory buzzes with new experiments, each a piece of Ral's ambitious project.", 'Feed on food, you eventually rot. Feed on rot, you live forever.\\n—Kraul saying', 'Few believe Duskmantle exists. Fewer find it. None live to bear witness.', 'First, dispose of the evidence. Then dispose of your knowledge of its disposal.', 'Fog haunts the streets, rendering the familiar as otherworldly, changing neighbors into shadows, and muffling cries for help.', 'From death she grows living grandeur.', "Genius is finding the edge of what's possible, then jumping over it.", 'Giants know a solid hit is one part strength, four parts leverage.', 'Golgari crops bloom in strange soils, touched only by long-traveled light.', 'Good at carrying things. Really good at knocking them down.', 'He ferried weapons, spells, exotic animals—but his most dangerous cargo was the truth.', "He has a job to finish, and it's you.", 'He heard stars and saw thunder.', 'In a climate of suspicion, Isperia gathered the guilds to propose a radical idea: cooperation.', 'In its territory, living is an affront.', 'In the Legion, no flagpole is merely decorative, and every ceremonial sword bears an edge.', 'In the quiet before a battle, Boros soldiers whisper prayers that steady their nerves and focus their minds.', "In the wake of Niv-Mizzet's disappearance, Ral found himself leading the guild. He had dreamed of this day, but couldn't help feeling like a pawn in someone else's game.", 'Its hyperpneumatics can punch through a wall and the spy on the other side.', 'Just assume every conversation is on record.', 'Made by the mad for the work of the wicked.', 'Nature\'s way of saying "take the long way home."', 'Nearly invisible strands of web reach far beyond its lair to alert it of the approach of prey.', 'No guilds—that is her rule. The House vampires unnerve her. The Combine would dissect her, the Legion burn her, the Conclave "cure" her. The shadows are all the family she needs.', 'No one welcomes his visit, yet all must grant him tribute.', "Once part of a wealthy merchant's private zoo, the herd roams feral throughout the Tenth, where it will remain until the guilds can agree to relocate, cull, or befriend it.", "Only the patrol's armor was found, so tainted with the acrid smell of sudden death that it could never be worn again.", 'Rain runoff in the Smelting District is known to spontaneously burst into flame.', 'Ral had wielded lightning all his life but had never harnessed the power of an entire guild.', "Ral's storm crackled with mystical detections: Planeswalkers were infiltrating Ravnica.", "Ravnica's convoluted power structure often boils down to who can muster the most swords on a given block.", "Ravnica's diversity produces blossoms of opinion in a rich soil of perspectives.", "Ravnica's safest strongholds are often neither.", "Rocs' innate fearlessness makes them ideal mounts for emergency response.", 'Rumors float through the city like crows, alighting on citizens seemingly at random.', 'Selesnya grows its ranks in more ways than one.', 'Selesnya guildmages do not sleep so the rest of the Conclave can.', 'She memorized every arcane text in the Ismeri Library by the time she was sixteen. Now she quizzes sphinxes in her spare time.', 'Some Gruul druids believe that boars are spawn of the great Ilharg, the mighty Raze-Boar who will one day rise and level the city.', 'Some rooftop gardens attract bees; others capture dragons.', 'Some storms never blow over.', 'Squadrons of skyknights are available for deployment around the clock, capable of reaching any district in the city within minutes.', "Suddenly, all the haggling didn't seem so important.", "The Boros banner stands tall even if its bearer doesn't.", 'The Chamber of the Guildpact stands as a reminder that even the bitterest struggles can end in cooperation.', 'The Dimir rarely make statements, but when they do, the message is clear.', "The Golgari adorn themselves with the exoskeletons of iridescent insects. It's only fair the insects do likewise.", 'The Izzet love replicating results.', 'The Izzet mage knew she would neither get her thermoinverter back nor have the satisfaction of exploding it herself.', 'The angels appreciated the offer but politely declined to eat any birdseed.', 'The assassins of the Ochran distill toxins from the remains of their previous victims.', 'The first thing the mist chills is the mind. Victims never cry out or even murmur in surprise.', 'The hive has a long memory. It knows how every member ever died, and to whom it owes the grudge.', "The kraul once skulked in the outskirts of Golgari society, but with Vraska's rise, they became valued forces of the Swarm.", 'The letters arrive, all sealed and read.', 'The party of Rakdos revelers cackled and capered as the thing approached. It hissed, and they jabbed their torches at it, giggling when it recoiled. Then, one by one, the torches went out—and the screaming began.', "The problem isn't the indrik's enthusiasm, it's Ravnica's lack of guardrails.", 'The sound of every twisted secret tempts you to hear another.', 'The ultimate answer to intrigue and subtlety.', 'The wounded see the glow of its vials long before they see its wings diving out of the clouds.', 'There are two lives: the life you live before you see a unicorn, and the life you live after.', "There's no greater honor than joining your chosen guild, and no greater shame than failing it.", 'Turns out coffee is the weird aunt of invention.', "What the Golgari can't claim through patient undercity expansion, they seize in brazen topside sorties.", 'When the Erstwhile were unearthed from their tombs, they became a ready-made army for Vraska.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Alayna Danner', 'Alex Konstad', 'Alexander Forssberg', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Ben Maier', 'Ben Wootten', 'Bram Sels', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Chris Seaman', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'David Palumbo', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Dimitar Marinski', 'Dmitry Burmak', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Even Amundsen', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'G-host Lee', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Greg Staples', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Heonhwa Choe', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Paick', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jedd Chevrier', 'Jehan Choo', 'Joe Slucher', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Thacker', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Josh Hass', 'Jung Park', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Kimonas Theodossiou', 'Kirsten Zirngibl', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Livia Prima', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Mark Behm', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Micah Epstein', 'Mike Bierek', 'Milivoj Ćeran', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paul Scott Canavan', 'Randy Vargas', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Richard Wright', 'Robbie Trevino', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Simon Dominic', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Sung Choi', 'Suzanne Helmigh', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Tianhua X', 'Titus Lunter', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tyler Walpole', 'Uriah Voth', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Winona Nelson', 'Wisnu Tan', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yongjae Choi', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros']
